{"hierarchy":{"paths":[[]]},"topicSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/DecisionDiagrams\/documentation\/DecisionDiagrams\/BinaryDecisionDiagram"],"anchor":"Binary-decision-diagrams","title":"Binary decision diagrams"},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/DecisionDiagrams\/documentation\/DecisionDiagrams\/ZeroSuppressedDecisionDiagram"],"anchor":"Zero-suppressed-decision-diagrams","title":"Zero-suppressed decision diagrams"}],"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"minor":3,"patch":0},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Canonical diagrams of Boolean functions and families of sets."}],"sections":[],"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/DecisionDiagrams\/documentation\/DecisionDiagrams"},"metadata":{"role":"collection","title":"DecisionDiagrams","modules":[{"name":"DecisionDiagrams"}],"externalID":"DecisionDiagrams","symbolKind":"module","roleHeading":"Framework"},"kind":"symbol","primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"level":2,"type":"heading","anchor":"Overview","text":"Overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/DecisionDiagrams\/documentation\/DecisionDiagrams\/BinaryDecisionDiagram","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" is a table of reduced ordered binary decision diagrams (Bryant,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"1986). Each function is a directed acyclic graph whose vertices test variables in index order,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"with a low child for the variable false and a high child for true, down to the constants. No two"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"vertices test the same variable with the same children, and none has equal children, so each"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"function has exactly one root, and checking whether two functions are equal is comparing roots."}]},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["import DecisionDiagrams","","var diagram = BinaryDecisionDiagram(variableCount: 3)","let x0 = diagram.variable(0), x1 = diagram.variable(1), x2 = diagram.variable(2)","let f = diagram.or(diagram.and(x0, x1), x2)   \/\/ x0 ∧ x1 ∨ x2","diagram.satisfyingAssignmentCount(of: f)       \/\/ 5","diagram.anySatisfyingAssignment(of: f)         \/\/ [false, false, true]"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The diagram of "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"f"},{"type":"text","text":" has five vertices: three tests and the two constants. Following the low edge"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"means the variable is false, the high edge that it is true."}]},{"type":"table","rows":[[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Vertex"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Tests","type":"text"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Low child","type":"text"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"High child","type":"text"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"root"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"x0"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"the test of "},{"code":"x2","type":"codeVoice"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"the test of "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"x1"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"x1","type":"codeVoice"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"the test of "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"x2"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"true"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"x2"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"false"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"true"}]}]]],"header":"row"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The test of ","type":"text"},{"code":"x2","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is shared: ","type":"text"},{"code":"x0","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" false and ","type":"text"},{"code":"x0 ∧ ¬x1","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" both leave ","type":"text"},{"code":"f","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" equal to ","type":"text"},{"code":"x2","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", so both lead","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"to the one vertex that stands for it.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Functions combine under any of the sixteen binary operators with"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/DecisionDiagrams\/documentation\/DecisionDiagrams\/BinaryDecisionDiagram\/apply(_:_:_:)"},{"type":"text","text":" in O(|"},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"text":"f","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":"| |"},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"g"}]},{"type":"text","text":"|), through a computed table of results"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"already found. "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/DecisionDiagrams\/documentation\/DecisionDiagrams\/BinaryDecisionDiagram\/restrict(_:variable:to:)"},{"type":"text","text":" fixes a variable, and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/DecisionDiagrams\/documentation\/DecisionDiagrams\/BinaryDecisionDiagram\/exists(_:in:)"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/DecisionDiagrams\/documentation\/DecisionDiagrams\/BinaryDecisionDiagram\/forall(_:in:)"},{"type":"text","text":" quantify"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"over variables. The table’s vertices are a "},{"code":"DirectedGraph","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/DecisionDiagrams\/documentation\/DecisionDiagrams\/BinaryDecisionDiagram\/graphView-swift.property"},{"type":"text","text":","},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"so Grafluent’s traversals and drawings run over a function’s diagram from its root."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"A ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/DecisionDiagrams\/documentation\/DecisionDiagrams\/ZeroSuppressedDecisionDiagram","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" is a table of families of sets (Minato, 1993). Its vertices","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"test elements in index order, with a low child for the sets without the element and a high child","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"for those with it. In place of the rule that removes a vertex with equal children, it removes one","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"whose high child is the empty family, so an element no set contains never appears in a diagram,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"and a sparse family over many elements stays small.","type":"text"}]},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["var diagram = ZeroSuppressedDecisionDiagram(elementCount: 3)","let f = diagram.family([[0, 1], [1, 2], [2]])","diagram.count(of: f)                                 \/\/ 3","diagram.minimalSets(of: diagram.including(2, in: f)) \/\/ {{2}}"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Families combine by "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/DecisionDiagrams\/documentation\/DecisionDiagrams\/ZeroSuppressedDecisionDiagram\/union(_:_:)"},{"type":"text","text":","},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/DecisionDiagrams\/documentation\/DecisionDiagrams\/ZeroSuppressedDecisionDiagram\/intersection(_:_:)"},{"type":"text","text":" and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/DecisionDiagrams\/documentation\/DecisionDiagrams\/ZeroSuppressedDecisionDiagram\/subtracting(_:from:)"},{"type":"text","text":", and set by set by"},{"type":"text","text":" "},